("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: The teacher said to the students, 'Do not make noise.'","The teacher told the students not to make noise.",["The teacher said the students not to make noise.","The teacher ordered the students do not make noise.","The teacher requested not making noise."],"Negative commands: 'told + object + not to + verb'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I bought this book yesterday.'","He said that he had bought that book the previous day.",["He said that he bought this book yesterday.","He said that he has bought this book yesterday.","He said that he had bought this book yesterday."],"'This' shifts to 'that', and 'yesterday' becomes 'the previous day'."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: She asked, 'Are you coming with me?'","She asked if/whether I was coming with her.",["She asked are you coming with me.","She asked that I was coming with her.","She asked if I am coming with her."],"Yes/no questions use 'if/whether' and standard tense-shift rules."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I shall come tomorrow.'","He said that he would come the next day.",["He said that he shall come tomorrow.","He said that he will come the next day.","He said that he would come tomorrow."],"'Shall' shifts to 'would'; 'tomorrow' becomes 'the next day'."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: The boy said, 'Alas! I have failed.'","The boy exclaimed with sorrow that he had failed.",["The boy said alas that he had failed.","The boy exclaimed that he has failed.","The boy said that he failed."],"'Alas!' expresses sorrow, reported with 'exclaimed with sorrow/grief that'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: She said, 'I saw him here.'","She said that she had seen him there.",["She said that she saw him here.","She said that she has seen him there.","She said that she had seen him here."],"'Here' shifts to 'there' along with the past-to-past-perfect tense shift."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'Let us go for a walk.'","He suggested that they should go for a walk.",["He said let us go for a walk.","He suggested going for a walk to them.","He told them let us go for a walk."],"Suggestions with 'let us' are reported as 'suggested that + subject + should'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: She said, 'I have never been to Paris.'","She said that she had never been to Paris.",["She said that she has never been to Paris.","She said that she never been to Paris.","She said that she was never in Paris."],"Present perfect ('have been') shifts to past perfect ('had been')."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I am going to finish this today.'","He said that he was going to finish that that day.",["He said that he is going to finish this today.","He said that he was going to finish this today.","He said that he had gone to finish that day."],"'This' → 'that' and 'today' → 'that day', with tense shift."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: The mother said to the child, 'Don't cry.'","The mother told the child not to cry.",["The mother said the child not to cry.","The mother requested the child don't cry.","The mother ordered do not cry."],"Negative imperative: 'told + object + not to + verb'."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I would help you if I could.'","He said that he would help me if he could.",["He said that he will help me if he can.","He said that he would help me if he can.","He said that he helped me if he could."],"Conditional sentences with 'would/could' generally remain unchanged in reported speech."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: She said, 'How clever you are!'","She exclaimed that I was very clever.",["She said how clever I am.","She exclaimed how clever I was.","She said that I was clever."],"Exclamations with 'how/what' are reported using 'exclaimed that + subject + was + very + adjective'."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: The captain said, 'We shall win this match.'","The captain said that they would win that match.",["The captain said that we shall win this match.","The captain said that they will win the match.","The captain said that they would win this match."],"'We' → 'they' (from the reporter's perspective), 'shall' → 'would', 'this' → 'that'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I do not like tea.'","He said that he did not like tea.",["He said that he does not like tea.","He said that he had not liked tea.","He said that he was not liking tea."],"Simple present negative shifts to simple past negative."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: She said to him, 'Will you marry me?'","She asked him if/whether he would marry her.",["She asked him will you marry me.","She asked him if he will marry her.","She said him if he would marry her."],"Reported yes/no questions with 'will' shift to 'would', introduced by 'if/whether'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: He said, 'I was sleeping when you called.'","He said that he had been sleeping when I had called.",["He said that he was sleeping when I called.","He said that he had been sleeping when I called.","He said that he is sleeping when I call."],"Past continuous generally shifts to past perfect continuous in strict tense-shift rules."),
("narration",2,"Change to indirect speech: The guide said, 'This temple was built in the 12th century.'","The guide said that that temple had been built in the 12th century.",["The guide said that this temple was built in the 12th century.","The guide said that the temple has been built in the 12th century.","The guide said that this temple had built in the 12th century."],"Historical facts still generally follow tense-shift rules unless treated as universal truths; 'this' → 'that'."),
("narration",1,"Change to indirect speech: She said, 'I shall not go there again.'","She said that she would not go there again.",["She said that she shall not go there again.","She said that she will not go there again.","She said that she would not go here again."],"'Shall not' → 'would not'; 'there' remains 'there' as the place reference is unchanged relative to speaker."),

# ---------------- SENTENCE / PARA SHUFFLING ----------------
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange the parts to form a meaningful sentence: P) to the market Q) went R) she S) yesterday","R Q P S",["R Q S P","S R Q P","Q R S P"],"Correct order: 'She went to the market yesterday.' — Subject, verb, object/place, time."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) is Q) the capital R) India S) of Delhi","Q R S is Delhi (i.e., 'Delhi is the capital of India')",["S is Q R","R S Q P","P Q S R"],"The correct sentence is 'Delhi is the capital of India' — subject first, then verb, then complement."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange the parts: P) his exam Q) worked hard R) he S) to pass","R Q S P",["R Q P S","Q R S P","S P R Q"],"'He worked hard to pass his exam' follows subject-verb-purpose-object order."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) a letter Q) she R) to her friend S) wrote","Q S P R",["Q S R P","S Q P R","P Q S R"],"'She wrote a letter to her friend' — subject, verb, direct object, indirect object phrase."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) every morning Q) the officer R) inspects S) the police station","Q R S P",["Q S R P","R Q S P","S Q R P"],"'The officer inspects the police station every morning' — subject, verb, object, time."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) is Q) important R) education S) for everyone","R P Q S",["S R P Q","P R Q S","R Q P S"],"'Education is important for everyone' — subject, verb, adjective, prepositional phrase."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) the plan Q) carefully R) they S) discussed","R S P Q",["R S Q P","S R P Q","P R S Q"],"'They discussed the plan carefully' follows subject-verb-object-adverb order."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) rises Q) in the east R) the sun","R P Q",["Q R P","P R Q","R Q P"],"'The sun rises in the east' — subject, verb, place."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) she Q) her homework R) before dinner S) completed","P S Q R",["P Q S R","S P Q R","P S R Q"],"'She completed her homework before dinner' — subject, verb, object, time."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) hard work Q) is the key R) to success","P Q R",["Q P R","R P Q","P R Q"],"'Hard work is the key to success' — subject, verb+complement, prepositional phrase."),
("shuffling",3,"Rearrange: P) despite the rain Q) the match R) continued S) as scheduled","P Q R S",["Q R P S","P R Q S","Q P R S"],"'Despite the rain, the match continued as scheduled' — the concessive phrase leads, then subject-verb-adverb."),
("shuffling",3,"Rearrange: P) has been Q) working hard R) she S) for months","R P Q S",["R Q P S","P R Q S","S R P Q"],"'She has been working hard for months' — subject, present perfect continuous verb, object/adverb, duration."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) went to Q) the constable R) the scene S) immediately","Q P R S",["Q P S R","R Q P S","Q R P S"],"'The constable went to the scene immediately' — subject, verb+place, time adverb."),
("shuffling",2,"Rearrange: P) is Q) a difficult subject R) mathematics","R P Q",["Q R P","P R Q","R Q P"],"'Mathematics is a difficult subject' — subject, verb, complement."),
("shuffling",3,"Rearrange: P) after completing Q) the training R) the recruits S) were deployed","P Q R S",["R S P Q","P R Q S","Q P R S"],"'After completing the training, the recruits were deployed' — introductory phrase, then subject-verb."),

